{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DYcTkXgdkK5fhMPHDwxjNx","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tnarrative_guidance: 'Reviewer panel 判定：(1) Theorem 1 bias identity 是 Carroll et al.\n2\t  (2006, Ch.4) 的 special case，不构成 novelty； (2) EC-HTE 在所有 real CM 场景中失败（exp-004 inconclusive,\n3\t  exp-015/016 negative），synthetic-only success = overfitting to DGP； (3) Diagnostic\n4\t  AUC=0.49 at setting level = coin flip，不可用； (4) A3 violation sensitivity（γ=0.1 coverage\n5\t  breakeven）在 real LLM 场景中几乎必然违反； (5) 整体贡献 = problem identification without working\n6\t  solution，不够 EMNLP main。 建议 reframe 为 empirical contribution paper：\"When Debiasing\n7\t  Hurts\"，放弃 method novelty claim， 转型为 large-scale empirical study of measurement error\n8\t  amplification。\n9\t\n10\t  '\n11\timagined_experiments:\n12\t- name: HB EC-HTE Synthetic Validation\n13\t  plan_id: exp-001\n14\t  description: Hierarchical Bayesian EC-HTE on synthetic data with full regime sweep\n15\t  expected_results:\n16\t    mcmc_rhat_max: 1.024\n17\t    mcmc_ess_min: 129\n18\t    total_mc_runs: 3600\n19\t    hb_vs_mle_rmse_improvement_k2_n50: 4-9%\n20\t    hb_vs_mle_rmse_improvement_k2_n100: 1-2%\n21\t    hb_vs_mle_rmse_improvement_k4_n50_moderate: 6-9%\n22\t    hb_coverage_median: 0.93\n23\t    hb_coverage_min: 0.87\n24\t    hyperprior_sensitivity_k4_rmse_variation: ~4-5%\n25\t    reviewer_perceived_novelty: none — standard James-Stein shrinkage\n26\t  result_rationale: 'Worst 档下，reviewer 完全承认 HB 在 synthetic 上 works，但判定： (a) 4-9% RMSE\n27\t    improvement over MLE 是 \"modest, well-known partial pooling benefit\"， 任何 Bayesian\n28\t    textbook 都有的 James-Stein shrinkage 效应； (b) synthetic DGP 是 symmetric misclassification（FPR=FNR），人为有利于\n29\t    CM inversion ——  real LLM misclassification 是 highly asymmetric（exp-004: FNR=53%），这使得\n30\t    synthetic 结果不可外推； (c) coverage 0.87-0.93 in worst configs 低于 nominal 0.95，但 reviewer\n31\t    不会 flag 这个 ——  他们的 attack vector 是 \"works on synthetic, fails on real\"，不是 synthetic\n32\t    内部的 calibration； (d) hyperprior sensitivity 4-5% 在 K=4 被视为 \"acceptable but unremarkable\"。\n33\t    总体判定：exp-001 是 competent engineering，不是 contribution。\n34\t\n35\t    '\n36\t  tables:\n37\t  - name: 'Table 1: HB vs MLE RMSE Comparison (Synthetic)'\n38\t    columns:\n39\t    - Config\n40\t    - HB RMSE\n41\t    - MLE RMSE\n42\t    - Delta %\n43\t    - Reviewer Verdict\n44\t    rows:\n45\t    - - K=2/extreme/n=50\n46\t      - '0.091'\n47\t      - '0.095'\n48\t      - -4.2%\n49\t      - '\"Modest, textbook shrinkage\"'\n50\t    - - K=2/extreme/n=100\n51\t      - '0.079'\n52\t      - '0.080'\n53\t      - -1.3%\n54\t      - '\"Negligible\"'\n55\t    - - K=4/extreme/n=50\n56\t      - '0.99'\n57\t      - '1.28'\n58\t      - -22.7%\n59\t      - '\"Only works because symmetric DGP\"'\n60\t    - - K=4/moderate/n=50\n61\t      - '0.14'\n62\t      - '0.15'\n63\t      - -6.7%\n64\t      - '\"Not replicable with real CMs\"'\n65\t  figures_description:\n66\t  - 'Reviewer 会要求 Fig: HB vs MLE RMSE across configs，但会注释 ''all synthetic, symmetric\n67\t    CMs — not informative for real deployment'''\n68\t  analysis: 'Reviewer 的核心 attack 不是 exp-001 结果本身不好，而是 synthetic-only validation  在\n69\t    exp-004/015/016 negative 结果面前失去说服力。exp-001 被重新定性为  \"method works under favorable\n70\t    assumptions that don''t hold in practice\"。 在 worst 档 reframe 下，exp-001 数据可以保留但重新定位为  \"controlled\n71\t    validation confirming implementation correctness\"，不再作为 method effectiveness 的\n72\t    evidence。\n73\t\n74\t    '\n75\t- name: Bias Identity Verification\n76\t  plan_id: exp-002\n77\t  description: 'Formal bias decomposition verification: bias = f(Δπ, Δτ) identity'\n78\t  expected_results:\n79\t    r2_k2: 0.9939\n80\t    r2_k4: 0.9738\n81\t    tightness_ratio_k2_median: 1.0027\n82\t    tightness_ratio_k4_median: 1.0234\n83\t    debiasing_hurts_pct: 50\n84\t    max_bias_ratio_k2: 2.86\n85\t    max_bias_ratio_k4: 2.41\n86\t    reviewer_novelty_assessment: textbook re-derivation\n87\t    carroll_overlap_pct: 85\n88\t  result_rationale: 'Worst 档的 defining assumption：reviewer panel 包含 measurement error\n89\t    专家，直接指出  Theorem 1 是 Carroll et al. (2006, Ch.4) 的 special case。具体论证： (a) \"bias\n90\t    ∝ Δπ × Δτ product form\" 是 classical ME literature 中 \"bias amplification  under\n91\t    misspecified correction model\" 的 well-known result，只是 notation 不同； (b) R² = 0.99\n92\t    证明 identity holds，但 \"verifying a known identity empirically\" 不是 contribution；\n93\t    (c) \"debiasing hurts in 50% of parameter space\" 被视为 \"trivially follows from the\n94\t    identity —  whenever Δπ and Δτ have the right sign combination, overcorrection\n95\t    occurs, this is Definition 4.2 in Carroll\"； (d) max bias ratio 2.86x / 2.41x 被视为\n96\t    \"interesting empirically but theoretically unsurprising\"； (e) K=2 vs K=4 non-monotonicity（2.86\n97\t    vs 2.41 for DIM）被视为 \"artifact of the specific estimator,  not a deep structural\n98\t    insight\"。 Reviewer 会写：\"The authors present Theorem 1 as a novel contribution,\n99\t    but the product-form  relationship between misclassification heterogeneity and\n100\t    bias amplification is a standard result  in the measurement error literature (Carroll\n101\t    et al. 2006, Fuller 1987). The empirical verification  with R²>0.97 is reassuring\n102\t    but not surprising.\"\n103\t\n104\t    '\n105\t  tables:\n106\t  - name: 'Table 2: Bias Identity R² and Reviewer Assessment'\n107\t    columns:\n108\t    - K\n109\t    - R²\n110\t    - Tightness Ratio\n111\t    - Reviewer Comment\n112\t    rows:\n113\t    - - '2'\n114\t      - '0.9939'\n115\t      - '1.0027'\n116\t      - '\"Exact — but this IS the classical result\"'\n117\t    - - '4'\n118\t      - '0.9738'\n119\t      - '1.0234'\n120\t      - '\"Slight deviation from identity = finite-sample noise, not new insight\"'\n121\t  - name: 'Table 3: Debiasing-Hurts Regions'\n122\t    columns:\n123\t    - Scenario\n124\t    - Bias Ratio\n125\t    - Δπ threshold\n126\t    - Reviewer Comment\n127\t    rows:\n128\t    - - K=2/extreme\n129\t      - 2.86x\n130\t      - '0.1235'\n131\t      - '\"Known: overcorrection when correction model misspecified\"'\n132\t    - - K=4/extreme\n133\t      - 2.41x\n134\t      - '0.1235'\n135\t      - '\"Same mechanism, different K\"'\n136\t    - - K=2/moderate\n137\t      - 1.2x\n138\t      - '0.1235'\n139\t      - '\"Marginal effect — who cares?\"'\n140\t  figures_description:\n141\t  - Δπ vs Δτ heatmap showing bias amplification — reviewer acknowledges visual clarity\n142\t    but annotates 'this is Fig 4.1 in Carroll (2006) applied to CATE'\n143\t  analysis: '这是 worst 档的 kill shot #1。当 measurement error 专家在 panel 上时， Theorem 1\n144\t    的 novelty claim 被直接否定。R² = 0.99 paradoxically 证明了这 IS 一个 known result  （如果是 novel，empirical\n145\t    verification 不该如此 clean）。 Reframe 方向：降级为 \"consistent with classical ME theory,\n146\t    we verify the product-form  identity holds empirically across LLM annotation settings\"，不再\n147\t    claim formal novelty。 关键：reframe 后这个 experiment 仍有价值，因为 \"verifying classical theory\n148\t    holds  in the LLM annotation context\" 是 valid empirical contribution，但需要 proper\n149\t    citation。\n150\t\n151\t    '\n152\t- name: Semi-Synthetic CSS Benchmark\n153\t  plan_id: exp-003\n154\t  description: Semi-synthetic benchmark using TweetEval sentiment with injected CATE\n155\t    structure\n156\t  expected_results:\n157\t    n_subgroups: 4\n158\t    misclass_rates: S0=0.05, S1=0.10, S2=0.15, S3=0.25\n159\t    p_z1_actual: 0.39\n160\t    debiasing_hurts_confirmed: true\n161\t    hb_vs_mle_n100_S3_extreme: +60% RMSE improvement\n162\t    hb_vs_mle_n50_S3_extreme: -57% RMSE (HB worse)\n163\t    boundary_condition: n_expert >= 100\n164\t    reviewer_perceived_validity: low — DGP designed to favor method\n165\t  result_rationale: 'Worst 档下 reviewer 对 exp-003 的攻击角度： (a) \"Semi-synthetic\" DGP 是\n166\t    author-designed：CATE heterogeneity 是 injected 的， misclassification rates 是 hand-picked\n167\t    的，treatment assignment 是 controlled 的 ——  \"the authors designed a DGP where their\n168\t    method works, then showed it works\"； (b) misclass_rates S0=0.05 到 S3=0.25 的 spread（Δπ=0.20）被视为\n169\t    \"optimistic —  real-world Δπ in exp-004 is only 0.117, and in exp-012 pilot is\n170\t    0.098-0.200 depending on grouping\"； (c) P(Z=1)=0.39 被视为 \"unrealistically high\n171\t    — CivilComments P(Z=1)=0.18,  most real datasets have severe class imbalance that\n172\t    exp-003 avoids\"； (d) n=50 boundary condition 被 acknowledged 但 n=100 recommendation\n173\t    被视为  \"will be violated in real per-subgroup settings with K=4+ and small expert\n174\t    budgets\"； (e) 整个 semi-synthetic 在 exp-015/016 negative 面前被 recharacterized 为  \"overfitting\n175\t    to favorable simulation conditions\"。\n176\t\n177\t    '\n178\t  tables:\n179\t  - name: 'Table 4: Semi-Synthetic Results vs Reviewer Perception'\n180\t    columns:\n181\t    - Config\n182\t    - HB RMSE Δ vs MLE\n183\t    - Actual Validity\n184\t    - Reviewer Perception\n185\t    rows:\n186\t    - - n=50/S3/extreme\n187\t      - -57%\n188\t      - Boundary condition\n189\t      - '\"Method fails at practical budgets\"'\n190\t    - - n=100/S3/extreme\n191\t      - +60%\n192\t      - Strong result\n193\t      - '\"Only works because P(Z=1)=0.39 and symmetric CM\"'\n194\t    - - n=250/S3\n195\t      - +5-17%\n196\t      - Moderate gain\n197\t      - '\"Modest, not worth the complexity\"'\n198\t    - - n=500/all\n199\t      - +0.2-1.6%\n200\t      - Converged\n201\t      - '\"At this budget, any method works\"'\n202\t  figures_description:\n203\t  - RMSE heatmap across n_expert × subgroup — reviewer annotates 'note P(Z=1)=0.39,\n204\t    unrealistic for most applications'\n205\t  analysis: 'exp-003 的 semi-synthetic 结果在 worst 档下被 reframed 为 \"controlled validation  that\n206\t    confirms implementation correctness under favorable conditions\"。 关键问题不是 exp-003\n207\t    结果错误，而是它不能 generalize： 当 P(Z=1) 从 0.39 降到 0.18（real data），per-subgroup expert\n208\t    labels  急剧减少，HB estimation noise 吞没 bias correction gain。 这 exactly 是 exp-015/016\n209\t    观察到的 pattern。Reviewer 将此称为 \"overfitting to simulation\"。\n210\t\n211\t    '\n212\t- name: Real-Data Case Study (Pattern Consistency)\n213\t  plan_id: exp-004\n214\t  description: Real CSS dataset (UC Berkeley Hate Speech) with subgroup-varying LLM\n215\t    misclassification\n216\t  expected_results:\n217\t    dataset: UC Berkeley Measuring Hate Speech\n218\t    n_comments: 2496\n219\t    delta_pi: 0.117\n220\t    global_FNR: 0.533\n221\t    avg_abs_bias_naive: 0.21\n222\t    avg_abs_bias_global: 0.273\n223\t    avg_abs_bias_ec_hte: 0.313\n224\t    ec_hte_worse_than_global: true\n225\t    ec_hte_worse_than_naive: true\n226\t    reviewer_verdict: fatal — method fails on real data\n227\t  result_rationale: '这是 worst 档的 kill shot #2，也是最具破坏力的 evidence。 Reviewer 论证链： (a)\n228\t    EC-HTE avg |bias| = 0.313 > Global 0.273 > Naive 0.21 ——  \"the proposed method\n229\t    is WORST among all options on real data\"； (b) 作者 frame 为 \"inconclusive due to\n230\t    wide bootstrap CIs\"，但 reviewer 反驳： \"wide CIs are themselves evidence of the method''s\n231\t    impracticality —  if you can''t get tight enough CIs to demonstrate improvement\n232\t    on 2496 samples,  the method doesn''t scale to realistic settings\"； (c) global\n233\t    FNR = 53% 被视为 \"typical of real LLM annotation\" 而非 \"edge case\" ——  \"if the method\n234\t    breaks whenever FNR > 0.4, it''s not useful for real NLP tasks  where LLMs systematically\n235\t    under-detect minority categories\"； (d) Δπ = 0.117 is \"moderate, not extreme\" ——\n236\t    \"the method needs extreme heterogeneity  to work, but real heterogeneity is moderate\"；\n237\t    (e) exp-015 (GPT-4.1 CMs) 和 exp-016 (GPT-3.5 CMs) 用 controlled semi-synthetic  确认了\n238\t    same failure pattern —— \"this is not a dataset artifact, it''s a systematic failure\"。\n239\t    Reviewer 会写：\"The real-data evaluation (Section 5.3) is the most informative result  in\n240\t    the paper, and it is negative. EC-HTE produces higher bias than both the naive\n241\t    estimator  and global correction on the UC Berkeley Hate Speech corpus. The authors\n242\t    attribute this  to high FNR, but high FNR is the norm in real LLM annotation tasks,\n243\t    not the exception.  A method that only works when the classifier is already good\n244\t    enough is of limited practical value.\"\n245\t\n246\t    '\n247\t  tables:\n248\t  - name: 'Table 5: Real-Data Results — The Fatal Evidence'\n249\t    columns:\n250\t    - Method\n251\t    - Avg |Bias|\n252\t    - Rank\n253\t    - Reviewer Interpretation\n254\t    rows:\n255\t    - - Naive\n256\t      - '0.210'\n257\t      - 1 (best)\n258\t      - '\"Doing nothing is better than the proposed method\"'\n259\t    - - Global Corrected\n260\t      - '0.273'\n261\t      - '2'\n262\t      - '\"Simple baseline outperforms\"'\n263\t    - - EC-HTE (proposed)\n264\t      - '0.313'\n265\t      - 3 (worst)\n266\t      - '\"Method INCREASES bias on real data\"'\n267\t  - name: 'Table 6: Cross-Validation with exp-015/016'\n268\t    columns:\n269\t    - Experiment\n270\t    - Real CMs Source\n271\t    - HB vs Global RMSE\n272\t    - Verdict\n273\t    rows:\n274\t    - - exp-004\n275\t      - UC Berkeley direct\n276\t      - HB worse\n277\t      - '\"Fatal\"'\n278\t    - - exp-015\n279\t      - GPT-4.1 pilot CMs\n280\t      - HB 3-4x worse\n281\t      - '\"Confirmed fatal\"'\n282\t    - - exp-016\n283\t      - GPT-3.5 CMs\n284\t      - HB 3.5-5x worse\n285\t      - '\"Triply confirmed\"'\n286\t  figures_description:\n287\t  - Per-subgroup bias comparison bar chart — EC-HTE bars consistently tallest, devastating\n288\t    visual\n289\t  analysis: 'exp-004 的 negative result 在 worst 档下无法 mitigate，只能 reframe。 Reframe 策略：这个\n290\t    negative result BECOMES the core contribution ——  \"we show that standard corrections\n291\t    fail on real data, and we characterize exactly  why (FNR > 0.4 + P(Z=1) < 0.2\n292\t    → insufficient per-subgroup positive-class expert labels)\"。 这是 \"When Debiasing\n293\t    Hurts\" 的 literal embodiment。 但 reviewer 的反驳是：\"problem identification without solution\n294\t    is not sufficient  for EMNLP main — you''ve shown the problem exists, now what?\"\n295\t\n296\t    '\n297\t- name: Diagnostic Criterion Validation\n298\t  plan_id: exp-005\n299\t  description: 'Diagnostic criterion: Δπ × Δτ predicts when global correction fails'\n300\t  expected_results:\n301\t    subgroup_level_auc: 0.833\n302\t    setting_level_auc: 0.49\n303\t    low_pi_hurt_pct: 84.6\n304\t    reviewer_verdict: contribution failure — AUC 0.49 at actionable level\n305\t  result_rationale: 'Worst 档的 kill shot #3。Reviewer 论证： (a) Setting-level AUC = 0.49\n306\t    是 \"literally worse than random\" ——  \"the diagnostic cannot predict at the level\n307\t    where practitioners need to make decisions  (should I use global or stratified\n308\t    correction for THIS dataset?)\"； (b) Subgroup-level AUC = 0.833 被 dismissed： \"subgroup-level\n309\t    prediction is not actionable — a practitioner doesn''t know true subgroup CATEs  at\n310\t    decision time, so they can''t compute the diagnostic at subgroup level\"； (c) \"84.6%\n311\t    of low-Δπ settings hurt\" 是 \"a marginal distribution, not a prediction\" ——  \"knowing\n312\t    that low heterogeneity settings tend to be hurt by correction is trivially obvious  from\n313\t    the bias identity; the diagnostic adds no information beyond the identity itself\"；\n314\t    (d) exp-028 进一步确认 asymmetric diagnostic 也 fails（overall AUC 0.626, K=2 all zero）；\n315\t    (e) reviewer 会将 Claim 3 标记为 \"not supported by the evidence\" 并要求删除或  大幅 downgrade。\n316\t    Reviewer 会写：\"The diagnostic criterion (Claim 3) is presented as a practical tool,  but\n317\t    its setting-level AUC of 0.49 means it cannot distinguish settings where global\n318\t    correction  helps from those where it hurts. The subgroup-level AUC of 0.833 is\n319\t    not actionable because  the required quantities (true subgroup CATEs) are unknown\n320\t    at decision time.  This contribution should be removed or reformulated as a negative\n321\t    result.\"\n322\t\n323\t    '\n324\t  tables:\n325\t  - name: 'Table 7: Diagnostic AUC — Claim vs Evidence'\n326\t    columns:\n327\t    - Level\n328\t    - AUC\n329\t    - Actionable?\n330\t    - Reviewer Verdict\n331\t    rows:\n332\t    - - Subgroup\n333\t      - '0.833'\n334\t      - No (requires true CATE)\n335\t      - '\"Circular — needs what you''re trying to estimate\"'\n336\t    - - Setting\n337\t      - '0.490'\n338\t      - Yes (but fails)\n339\t      - '\"Worse than coin flip\"'\n340\t    - - Asymmetric (exp-028)\n341\t      - 0.611-0.626\n342\t      - 'No'\n343\t      - '\"Marginal improvement, still useless\"'\n344\t  figures_description:\n345\t  - ROC curve at setting level — curve hugs diagonal, visually devastating\n346\t  analysis: 'Diagnostic 在 worst 档下被判定为 complete failure。 Reframe 策略：abandon AUC-based\n347\t    prediction entirely，转为  \"empirical rule of thumb: if Δπ > 0.10, check before applying\n348\t    global correction\"。 这不是 formal diagnostic，而是 practitioner guideline ——  类似 \"if\n349\t    VIF > 10, worry about multicollinearity\" 的 heuristic。 但 reviewer 可能仍会质疑：\"this\n350\t    threshold was derived from your own synthetic data,  how do we know it generalizes?\"\n351\t\n352\t    '\n353\t- name: Expert Label Budget Sensitivity\n354\t  plan_id: exp-006\n355\t  description: Systematic sweep of n_expert × K × regime for crossover point\n356\t  expected_results:\n357\t    crossover_K2_extreme: 250\n358\t    crossover_K2_moderate: never\n359\t    crossover_K4_extreme: 1000\n360\t    crossover_K4_moderate: 2000\n361\t    hb_vs_mle_wins: 21/24 (87.5%)\n362\t    reviewer_verdict: impractical budgets in moderate regime\n363\t  result_rationale: 'Worst 档下 reviewer 的解读： (a) K=2/moderate \"never crosses\" = \"in\n364\t    the most common real-world scenario  (moderate heterogeneity, binary subgroups),\n365\t    EC-HTE NEVER outperforms global on RMSE\"； (b) K=4/extreme crossover at n=1000\n366\t    experts = \"who has 1000 expert-labeled samples  for calibration? At that budget,\n367\t    just use expert labels directly for CATE estimation\"； (c) K=4/moderate crossover\n368\t    at n=2000 = \"absurd — 2000 expert labels for 4 subgroups  means 500/subgroup,\n369\t    at which point expert-only estimation is viable\"； (d) K=2/extreme crossover at\n370\t    n=250 是 \"the only practical scenario,  but extreme heterogeneity is rare in real\n371\t    data (exp-004 Δπ=0.117 is moderate)\"； (e) HB vs MLE 21/24 wins 被 dismissed as\n372\t    \"improvement over the wrong baseline —  the question is HB vs Global, not HB vs\n373\t    MLE\"。 总结：reviewer 将 exp-006 解读为 \"the method''s own budget analysis shows  it''s\n374\t    impractical except in rare extreme-heterogeneity scenarios\"。\n375\t\n376\t    '\n377\t  tables:\n378\t  - name: 'Table 8: Crossover Points — Reviewer Interpretation'\n379\t    columns:\n380\t    - Config\n381\t    - Crossover n_expert\n382\t    - Practical?\n383\t    - Reviewer Comment\n384\t    rows:\n385\t    - - K=2/extreme\n386\t      - '250'\n387\t      - Marginal\n388\t      - '\"Only practical scenario, but extreme regime is rare\"'\n389\t    - - K=2/moderate\n390\t      - Never\n391\t      - 'No'\n392\t      - '\"Method never helps in common scenario\"'\n393\t    - - K=4/extreme\n394\t      - '1000'\n395\t      - 'No'\n396\t      - '\"Budget exceeds most research projects\"'\n397\t    - - K=4/moderate\n398\t      - '2000'\n399\t      - 'No'\n400\t      - '\"At 2000 labels, use experts directly\"'\n401\t  figures_description:\n402\t  - Crossover curve plot — reviewer highlights the 'never' line for K=2/moderate as\n403\t    paper's self-contradiction\n404\t  analysis: 'exp-006 在 worst 档下成为 \"method''s own evidence against itself\"。 核心问题：EC-HTE\n405\t    的 value proposition 是 \"use LLM labels cheaply + few expert labels for calibration\"，\n406\t    但 crossover analysis 显示 calibration 本身需要大量 expert labels， 侵蚀了 cost-effectiveness\n407\t    argument。 Reframe：转为 \"budget guidelines for practitioners\" —— 不是 \"EC-HTE 需要多少\n408\t    labels\"  而是 \"any correction method 在低 budget 时不如 naive\"。\n409\t\n410\t    '\n411\t- name: PPCI + DSL Baseline Comparison\n412\t  plan_id: exp-007\n413\t  description: PPCI/DSL baselines, EC-HTE+PPCI composition for dual-error scenarios\n414\t  expected_results:\n415\t    dgp_c_extreme_n250_k2_ec_hte_ppci_bias: 0.005\n416\t    dgp_c_extreme_n250_k2_ppci_alone_bias: 0.004\n417\t    dgp_c_extreme_n250_k2_ec_hte_alone_bias: 0.178\n418\t    ec_hte_ppci_rmse: 0.225\n419\t    ppci_alone_rmse: 0.261\n420\t    reviewer_verdict: PPCI alone achieves same bias reduction — why add EC-HTE?\n421\t  result_rationale: 'Worst 档下 reviewer 的 devastating observation： (a) DGP C（both errors）:\n422\t    ec_hte_ppci bias = 0.005, BUT ppci_alone bias = 0.004 ——  \"PPCI alone achieves\n423\t    LOWER bias than the proposed composition! EC-HTE adds nothing to bias reduction\"；\n424\t    (b) RMSE: ec_hte_ppci 0.225 vs ppci_alone 0.261 = 14% improvement， 但 reviewer\n425\t    认为 \"this modest RMSE gain doesn''t justify the additional complexity  of implementing\n426\t    EC-HTE on top of PPCI\"； (c) DGP A（covariate only）: ec_hte works well，但 reviewer\n427\t    质疑： \"how often is covariate error the ONLY error source? In real data, outcome\n428\t    error always exists， making DGP C the relevant scenario — where PPCI alone suffices\"；\n429\t    (d) DSL per-subgroup 作为 baseline 未被 properly compared： \"if DSL per-subgroup achieves\n430\t    comparable results without the HB machinery,  what''s the methodological contribution?\"；\n431\t    (e) \"Composition is necessary and sufficient\" claim 被 weakened to  \"PPCI is sufficient;\n432\t    EC-HTE is optional for modest RMSE gains\"。\n433\t\n434\t    '\n435\t  tables:\n436\t  - name: 'Table 9: DGP C (Both Errors) — PPCI vs EC-HTE+PPCI'\n437\t    columns:\n438\t    - Method\n439\t    - '|Bias|'\n440\t    - RMSE\n441\t    - Reviewer Verdict\n442\t    rows:\n443\t    - - PPCI alone\n444\t      - '0.004'\n445\t      - '0.261'\n446\t      - '\"Sufficient — simpler, nearly same bias\"'\n447\t    - - EC-HTE+PPCI\n448\t      - '0.005'\n449\t      - '0.225'\n450\t      - '\"Marginal RMSE gain, not worth complexity\"'\n451\t    - - EC-HTE alone\n452\t      - '0.178'\n453\t      - '0.226'\n454\t      - '\"Cannot handle outcome error\"'\n455\t    - - Naive\n456\t      - '0.251'\n457\t      - '0.269'\n458\t      - '\"EC-HTE alone barely beats naive\"'\n459\t  figures_description:\n460\t  - DGP A/B/C comparison panel — reviewer circles DGP C where PPCI alone ≈ EC-HTE+PPCI\n461\t  analysis: 'exp-007 在 worst 档下暴露了 EC-HTE 的 marginal value： 当 PPCI 已经 available 时，EC-HTE\n462\t    的 additional contribution 仅是 14% RMSE reduction。 Reviewer 将此定性为 \"incremental improvement\n463\t    over existing method,  not a new paradigm\"。 Reframe：在 \"When Debiasing Hurts\" 版本中，PPCI\n464\t    comparison  成为 \"what practitioners should use instead\" 的 recommendation。\n465\t\n466\t    '\n467\t- name: Multiple LLM Annotator Comparison\n468\t  plan_id: exp-008\n469\t  description: 6 LLM models (GPT-3.5 through GPT-5.4) measuring misclassification\n470\t    heterogeneity patterns\n471\t  expected_results:\n472\t    models_completed: 6\n473\t    all_delta_pi_above_005: true\n474\t    effective_delta_pi_range: 0.080 - 0.198\n475\t    worst_subgroup_consensus: True_medium (5/6 models)\n476\t    spearman_significant_pairs: 4\n477\t    reviewer_verdict: unsurprising — well-known that different models have different\n478\t      error patterns\n479\t  result_rationale: 'Worst 档下 reviewer 承认 empirical finding 但否定其 significance： (a)\n480\t    \"All 6 models show Δπ > 0.05\" 被视为 \"we already know LLMs have non-uniform error\n481\t    patterns —  Ashwin et al. (2025) documented this, Tornberg (2024) documented this,  the\n482\t    entire LLM-as-annotator literature is built on this observation\"； (b) Δπ range\n483\t    0.080-0.198 被视为 \"moderate, not extreme — confirming that  real-world heterogeneity\n484\t    falls in the regime where EC-HTE doesn''t help (exp-006: K=2/moderate never crosses)\"；\n485\t    (c) \"Structural, not model-specific\" finding 被 reviewer 重新 frame： \"yes, heterogeneity\n486\t    is structural — and it''s structurally MODERATE,  which is exactly the regime\n487\t    where global correction is sufficient\"； (d) 只有 4 subgroups after filtering（excluding\n488\t    n<10），statistical power 有限， Spearman correlations 多数 p>0.20； (e) GPT-5.4 Δπ=0.114\n489\t    被 reviewer 引用为 \"even the best available model  has moderate heterogeneity — confirming\n490\t    that the MODERATE regime is the relevant one\"。 然而在 reframed \"When Debiasing Hurts\"\n491\t    版本中，exp-008 成为 core contribution： 6 models × 3 generations 的 systematic evidence\n492\t    证明 heterogeneity 是 structural phenomenon。\n493\t\n494\t    '\n495\t  tables:\n496\t  - name: 'Table 10: Cross-Model Δπ — Reviewer Interpretation'\n497\t    columns:\n498\t    - Model\n499\t    - Generation\n500\t    - Effective Δπ\n501\t    - Reviewer Comment\n502\t    rows:\n503\t    - - GPT-3.5-turbo\n504\t      - Gen 1\n505\t      - '0.198'\n506\t      - '\"Oldest model, most error — unsurprising\"'\n507\t    - - GPT-4-turbo\n508\t      - Gen 2\n509\t      - '0.149'\n510\t      - '\"Better model, less error — unsurprising\"'\n511\t    - - GPT-4.1\n512\t      - Gen 2\n513\t      - '0.098'\n514\t      - '\"Moderate — in the regime where EC-HTE doesn''t help\"'\n515\t    - - GPT-4o\n516\t      - Gen 2\n517\t      - '0.080'\n518\t      - '\"Low — global correction sufficient\"'\n519\t    - - GPT-4o-mini\n520\t      - Gen 2\n521\t      - '0.136'\n522\t      - '\"Small model, more error — expected\"'\n523\t    - - GPT-5.4\n524\t      - Gen 3\n525\t      - '0.114'\n526\t      - '\"Latest model still has moderate heterogeneity\"'\n527\t  figures_description:\n528\t  - Bar chart of Δπ across 6 models, ordered by generation — reviewer notes downward\n529\t    trend as evidence 'problem is diminishing with model improvement'\n530\t  analysis: 'exp-008 在 worst 档下有双重解读： (1) Reviewer 可以 argue \"heterogeneity is diminishing\n531\t    with model generations  (GPT-3.5: 0.198 → GPT-5.4: 0.114), so the problem is self-solving\"；\n532\t    (2) 但在 reframed paper 中，这 IS the contribution：systematic evidence  across 6 models\n533\t    showing heterogeneity persists even in latest generation。 关键防御：Δπ=0.114 for GPT-5.4\n534\t    仍然 above the threshold（0.10） where bias amplification is non-trivial。\n535\t\n536\t    '\n537\t- name: Adaptive Expert Annotation Allocation\n538\t  plan_id: exp-009\n539\t  description: CATE-weighted allocation targeting high-CATE × high-error subgroups\n540\t  expected_results:\n541\t    status: not completed (P2 priority, cut from submission)\n542\t    reviewer_reaction: missing experiment noted but not fatal\n543\t    hypothetical_if_run:\n544\t      improvement_over_uniform: 10-15% RMSE reduction in high-error subgroups\n545\t      aggregate_improvement: 5-8% overall\n546\t      still_worse_than_global_in_moderate: true\n547\t  result_rationale: 'Worst 档下 exp-009 大概率未完成（P2 priority，5-day deadline 内无法实现）。 Reviewer\n548\t    反应分两种： (a) 如果提到但未完成：\"the authors mention adaptive allocation as future work,  but\n549\t    this would be necessary to make the method practical — without it,  the budget\n550\t    requirements (exp-006) are prohibitive\"； (b) 如果完全不提：reviewer 不会注意到缺失，因为 exp-009\n551\t    不是 core claim 的 evidence。 即使 exp-009 完成，worst 档 reviewer 仍会 argue： \"adaptive allocation\n552\t    improves EC-HTE but doesn''t change the fundamental conclusion —  the method requires\n553\t    too many expert labels to be practical\"。 在 reframed paper 中，exp-009 可以作为 appendix-level\n554\t    future direction， 但不影响 core empirical contribution。\n555\t\n556\t    '\n557\t  tables:\n558\t  - name: 'Table 11: Adaptive Allocation (Hypothetical)'\n559\t    columns:\n560\t    - Allocation\n561\t    - Aggregate RMSE\n562\t    - High-Error Subgroup RMSE\n563\t    - Reviewer Verdict\n564\t    rows:\n565\t    - - Uniform\n566\t      - '0.12'\n567\t      - '0.18'\n568\t      - '\"Baseline\"'\n569\t    - - CATE-weighted\n570\t      - '0.11'\n571\t      - '0.15'\n572\t      - '\"Modest improvement, doesn''t fix fundamental issue\"'\n573\t    - - Uncertainty-only\n574\t      - '0.115'\n575\t      - '0.16'\n576\t      - '\"Similar to CATE-weighted\"'\n577\t  figures_description:\n578\t  - Not generated — experiment cut from submission\n579\t  analysis: 'exp-009 的缺失在 worst 档下不是 major weakness，因为 reviewer 的 attack vector  是\n580\t    \"method doesn''t work on real data\" 而非 \"method could be improved with adaptive\n581\t    allocation\"。 Cutting exp-009 is correct under time constraints。\n582\t\n583\t    '\n584\t- name: Robustness to Misspecified Subgroup Structure\n585\t  plan_id: exp-010\n586\t  description: Test EC-HTE when subgroups are noisy/overlapping\n587\t  expected_results:\n588\t    k2_coverage_hb_noise0: 0.958\n589\t    k2_coverage_hb_noise50: 0.945\n590\t    k4_coverage_hb_noise0: 0.956\n591\t    k4_coverage_hb_noise50: 0.946\n592\t    graceful_convergence: true\n593\t    hb_beats_mle_all_configs: true\n594\t    reviewer_verdict: trivial result — HB shrinkage is known to be robust\n595\t  result_rationale: 'Worst 档下 reviewer 对 exp-010 的评价： (a) \"Coverage maintained at\n596\t    94.5-95.8% across all noise levels\" 被视为  \"this is the well-known property of hierarchical\n597\t    Bayesian shrinkage —  it automatically pools toward the global estimate when subgroup\n598\t    signal is noisy,  providing an automatic safeguard. This is not a finding, it''s\n599\t    a property of the method\"； (b) \"Graceful convergence to global at 50% noise\" 是\n600\t    \"by construction —  when subgroup labels are random, HB posterior concentrates\n601\t    on the global mean.  This is Definition 1 of partial pooling\"； (c) reviewer 不会\n602\t    flag exp-010 as weakness，但 also 不会 credit it as contribution ——  it''s \"expected\n603\t    behavior, properly verified but not interesting\"； (d) 在 worst 档下，exp-010 的 robustness\n604\t    evidence 被 counter-argued by  exp-015/016/030：\"robust to noise is not the same\n605\t    as robust to real-world conditions —  the method gracefully degrades to Global\n606\t    (the thing it was supposed to beat)\"。\n607\t\n608\t    '\n609\t  tables:\n610\t  - name: 'Table 12: Robustness — Coverage Across Noise Levels'\n611\t    columns:\n612\t    - Noise Level\n613\t    - K=2 HB Coverage\n614\t    - K=4 HB Coverage\n615\t    - Reviewer Comment\n616\t    rows:\n617\t    - - 0%\n618\t      - '0.958'\n619\t      - '0.956'\n620\t      - '\"Nominal — as expected\"'\n621\t    - - 10%\n622\t      - '0.948'\n623\t      - '0.958'\n624\t      - '\"Robust — as expected from HB\"'\n625\t    - - 25%\n626\t      - '0.950'\n627\t      - '0.960'\n628\t      - '\"Still nominal — standard shrinkage property\"'\n629\t    - - 50%\n630\t      - '0.945'\n631\t      - '0.946'\n632\t      - '\"Converges to global — by construction\"'\n633\t  figures_description:\n634\t  - Coverage vs noise level — flat line, 'reassuring but uninformative' per reviewer\n635\t  analysis: 'exp-010 在 worst 档下是 neutral evidence：不帮助也不伤害。 Reviewer 认为 robustness\n636\t    to subgroup noise 是 \"expected baseline behavior,  not a contribution\"。在 reframed\n637\t    paper 中可以保留在 appendix  作为 \"implementation validation\" 但不宜放在 main text。\n638\t\n639\t    '\n640\t- name: Causal Forest Integration\n641\t  plan_id: exp-011\n642\t  description: 'EC-HTE with CausalForestDML: bias reduction + debiasing-hurts amplification'\n643\t  expected_results:\n644\t    mean_abs_bias_naive: 0.1558\n645\t    mean_abs_bias_global: 0.1073\n646\t    mean_abs_bias_ec_hte: 0.0608\n647\t    mean_rmse_naive: 0.1782\n648\t    mean_rmse_global: 0.1659\n649\t    mean_rmse_ec_hte: 0.2289\n650\t    debiasing_hurts_max_ratio: 5.9\n651\t    debiasing_hurts_cases: 9\n652\t    reviewer_verdict: bias-variance tradeoff unfavorable — RMSE 38% worse than global\n653\t  result_rationale: 'Worst 档下 reviewer 对 exp-011 的解读高度 adversarial： (a) EC-HTE RMSE\n654\t    = 0.2289 vs Global RMSE = 0.1659 —— \"EC-HTE has 38% HIGHER RMSE  than global correction\n655\t    when combined with CausalForest. Lower bias comes at  unacceptable variance cost\"；\n656\t    (b) \"A practitioner cares about RMSE (combined bias + variance), not bias alone.  EC-HTE\n657\t    trades manageable bias for enormous variance, making estimates LESS useful\"； (c)\n658\t    5.9x debiasing-hurts ratio 被 dual-interpreted： reviewer 承认 \"global correction\n659\t    can dramatically amplify bias with CausalForest\"  但 adds \"EC-HTE doesn''t fix\n660\t    this — it has even worse RMSE, just distributed differently  (lower bias, higher\n661\t    variance)\"； (d) 9 cases of debiasing-hurts 在 144 total rows = 6.25%，被视为  \"rare\n662\t    enough that practitioners can detect and handle manually\"； (e) K=2/n=500 near-zero\n663\t    bias（0.004-0.013）被 acknowledged 但  \"at n=500 per subgroup, the expert budget is\n664\t    no longer small —  1000+ experts for 2 subgroups exceeds most research budgets\"。\n665\t    Reviewer 会写：\"Table 4 reveals that EC-HTE''s bias reduction comes at a steep  variance\n666\t    cost: mean RMSE increases 38% compared to global correction (0.229 vs 0.166).  For\n667\t    practitioners who care about prediction accuracy (not just unbiasedness),  this\n668\t    tradeoff is unfavorable. The 5.9x debiasing-hurts ratio for K=4/extreme  is concerning\n669\t    but occurs in only 6% of configurations.\"\n670\t\n671\t    '\n672\t  tables:\n673\t  - name: 'Table 13: CausalForest — Bias vs RMSE Tradeoff'\n674\t    columns:\n675\t    - Method\n676\t    - Mean |Bias|\n677\t    - Mean RMSE\n678\t    - RMSE Rank\n679\t    - Reviewer Verdict\n680\t    rows:\n681\t    - - Naive\n682\t      - '0.156'\n683\t      - '0.178'\n684\t      - '2'\n685\t      - '\"Higher bias but lower RMSE than EC-HTE\"'\n686\t    - - Global\n687\t      - '0.107'\n688\t      - '0.166'\n689\t      - 1 (best)\n690\t      - '\"Best RMSE, acceptable bias\"'\n691\t    - - EC-HTE\n692\t      - '0.061'\n693\t      - '0.229'\n694\t      - 3 (worst)\n695\t      - '\"Lowest bias but worst RMSE — unfavorable tradeoff\"'\n696\t  - name: 'Table 14: Debiasing-Hurts Cases with CausalForest'\n697\t    columns:\n698\t    - Config\n699\t    - Global/Naive Bias Ratio\n700\t    - Frequency\n701\t    - Reviewer Comment\n702\t    rows:\n703\t    - - K=4/extreme/sg0\n704\t      - 5.9x\n705\t      - 1/144\n706\t      - '\"Rare extreme case\"'\n707\t    - - K=4/extreme/sg1-3\n708\t      - 1.2-2.1x\n709\t      - 8/144\n710\t      - '\"Moderate, manageable\"'\n711\t    - - All other configs\n712\t      - <1.0x\n713\t      - 135/144\n714\t      - '\"Global correction works fine 94% of the time\"'\n715\t  figures_description:\n716\t  - Bias-RMSE scatterplot with method colors — EC-HTE in Pareto-dominated region (low\n717\t    bias, high RMSE)\n718\t  analysis: exp-011 在 worst 档下强化了 \"method works in theory, fails in practice\" narrative：\n719\t    即使在 synthetic DGP 上，EC-HTE 的 RMSE 比 global 差 38%。 Reviewer 将此解读为 \"the fundamental\n720\t    tradeoff is unfavorable —  per-subgroup CM estimation noise exceeds the bias correction\n721\t    benefit\"。 在 reframed paper 中，5.9x debiasing-hurts 成为 core empirical finding： \"CausalForest\n722\t    amplifies the debiasing-hurts effect\" 是 novel observation， 但需要 frame 为 \"warning\n723\t    to practitioners\" 而非 \"EC-HTE solves this\"。\n724\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"44ebc33a-5f0e-4594-9646-2fa2afa29759","uuid":"3f855123-74c8-4cf4-93f6-31ed88d5ab5c","timestamp":"2026-05-23T20:27:26.813Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0520/projects/ec_hte_llm_annotation/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260523T193110/worst/review_context.yaml","content":"narrative_guidance: 'Reviewer panel 判定：(1) Theorem 1 bias identity 是 Carroll et al.\n  (2006, Ch.4) 的 special case，不构成 novelty； (2) EC-HTE 在所有 real CM 场景中失败（exp-004 inconclusive,\n  exp-015/016 negative），synthetic-only success = overfitting to DGP； (3) Diagnostic\n  AUC=0.49 at setting level = coin flip，不可用； (4) A3 violation sensitivity（γ=0.1 coverage\n  breakeven）在 real LLM 场景中几乎必然违反； (5) 整体贡献 = problem identification without working\n  solution，不够 EMNLP main。 建议 reframe 为 empirical contribution paper：\"When Debiasing\n  Hurts\"，放弃 method novelty claim， 转型为 large-scale empirical study of measurement error\n  amplification。\n\n  '\nimagined_experiments:\n- name: HB EC-HTE Synthetic Validation\n  plan_id: exp-001\n  description: Hierarchical Bayesian EC-HTE on synthetic data with full regime sweep\n  expected_results:\n    mcmc_rhat_max: 1.024\n    mcmc_ess_min: 129\n    total_mc_runs: 3600\n    hb_vs_mle_rmse_improvement_k2_n50: 4-9%\n    hb_vs_mle_rmse_improvement_k2_n100: 1-2%\n    hb_vs_mle_rmse_improvement_k4_n50_moderate: 6-9%\n    hb_coverage_median: 0.93\n    hb_coverage_min: 0.87\n    hyperprior_sensitivity_k4_rmse_variation: ~4-5%\n    reviewer_perceived_novelty: none — standard James-Stein shrinkage\n  result_rationale: 'Worst 档下，reviewer 完全承认 HB 在 synthetic 上 works，但判定： (a) 4-9% RMSE\n    improvement over MLE 是 \"modest, well-known partial pooling benefit\"， 任何 Bayesian\n    textbook 都有的 James-Stein shrinkage 效应； (b) synthetic DGP 是 symmetric misclassification（FPR=FNR），人为有利于\n    CM inversion ——  real LLM misclassification 是 highly asymmetric（exp-004: FNR=53%），这使得\n    synthetic 结果不可外推； (c) coverage 0.87-0.93 in worst configs 低于 nominal 0.95，但 reviewer\n    不会 flag 这个 ——  他们的 attack vector 是 \"works on synthetic, fails on real\"，不是 synthetic\n    内部的 calibration； (d) hyperprior sensitivity 4-5% 在 K=4 被视为 \"acceptable but unremarkable\"。\n    总体判定：exp-001 是 competent engineering，不是 contribution。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table 1: HB vs MLE RMSE Comparison (Synthetic)'\n    columns:\n    - Config\n    - HB RMSE\n    - MLE RMSE\n    - Delta %\n    - Reviewer Verdict\n    rows:\n    - - K=2/extreme/n=50\n      - '0.091'\n      - '0.095'\n      - -4.2%\n      - '\"Modest, textbook shrinkage\"'\n    - - K=2/extreme/n=100\n      - '0.079'\n      - '0.080'\n      - -1.3%\n      - '\"Negligible\"'\n    - - K=4/extreme/n=50\n      - '0.99'\n      - '1.28'\n      - -22.7%\n      - '\"Only works because symmetric DGP\"'\n    - - K=4/moderate/n=50\n      - '0.14'\n      - '0.15'\n      - -6.7%\n      - '\"Not replicable with real CMs\"'\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Reviewer 会要求 Fig: HB vs MLE RMSE across configs，但会注释 ''all synthetic, symmetric\n    CMs — not informative for real deployment'''\n  analysis: 'Reviewer 的核心 attack 不是 exp-001 结果本身不好，而是 synthetic-only validation  在\n    exp-004/015/016 negative 结果面前失去说服力。exp-001 被重新定性为  \"method works under favorable\n    assumptions that don''t hold in practice\"。 在 worst 档 reframe 下，exp-001 数据可以保留但重新定位为  \"controlled\n    validation confirming implementation correctness\"，不再作为 method effectiveness 的\n    evidence。\n\n    '\n- name: Bias Identity Verification\n  plan_id: exp-002\n  description: 'Formal bias decomposition verification: bias = f(Δπ, Δτ) identity'\n  expected_results:\n    r2_k2: 0.9939\n    r2_k4: 0.9738\n    tightness_ratio_k2_median: 1.0027\n    tightness_ratio_k4_median: 1.0234\n    debiasing_hurts_pct: 50\n    max_bias_ratio_k2: 2.86\n    max_bias_ratio_k4: 2.41\n    reviewer_novelty_assessment: textbook re-derivation\n    carroll_overlap_pct: 85\n  result_rationale: 'Worst 档的 defining assumption：reviewer panel 包含 measurement error\n    专家，直接指出  Theorem 1 是 Carroll et al. (2006, Ch.4) 的 special case。具体论证： (a) \"bias\n    ∝ Δπ × Δτ product form\" 是 classical ME literature 中 \"bias amplification  under\n    misspecified correction model\" 的 well-known result，只是 notation 不同； (b) R² = 0.99\n    证明 identity holds，但 \"verifying a known identity empirically\" 不是 contribution；\n    (c) \"debiasing hurts in 50% of parameter space\" 被视为 \"trivially follows from the\n    identity —  whenever Δπ and Δτ have the right sign combination, overcorrection\n    occurs, this is Definition 4.2 in Carroll\"； (d) max bias ratio 2.86x / 2.41x 被视为\n    \"interesting empirically but theoretically unsurprising\"； (e) K=2 vs K=4 non-monotonicity（2.86\n    vs 2.41 for DIM）被视为 \"artifact of the specific estimator,  not a deep structural\n    insight\"。 Reviewer 会写：\"The authors present Theorem 1 as a novel contribution,\n    but the product-form  relationship between misclassification heterogeneity and\n    bias amplification is a standard result  in the measurement error literature (Carroll\n    et al. 2006, Fuller 1987). The empirical verification  with R²>0.97 is reassuring\n    but not surprising.\"\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table 2: Bias Identity R² and Reviewer Assessment'\n    columns:\n    - K\n    - R²\n    - Tightness Ratio\n    - Reviewer Comment\n    rows:\n    - - '2'\n      - '0.9939'\n      - '1.0027'\n      - '\"Exact — but this IS the classical result\"'\n    - - '4'\n      - '0.9738'\n      - '1.0234'\n      - '\"Slight deviation from identity = finite-sample noise, not new insight\"'\n  - name: 'Table 3: Debiasing-Hurts Regions'\n    columns:\n    - Scenario\n    - Bias Ratio\n    - Δπ threshold\n    - Reviewer Comment\n    rows:\n    - - K=2/extreme\n      - 2.86x\n      - '0.1235'\n      - '\"Known: overcorrection when correction model misspecified\"'\n    - - K=4/extreme\n      - 2.41x\n      - '0.1235'\n      - '\"Same mechanism, different K\"'\n    - - K=2/moderate\n      - 1.2x\n      - '0.1235'\n      - '\"Marginal effect — who cares?\"'\n  figures_description:\n  - Δπ vs Δτ heatmap showing bias amplification — reviewer acknowledges visual clarity\n    but annotates 'this is Fig 4.1 in Carroll (2006) applied to CATE'\n  analysis: '这是 worst 档的 kill shot #1。当 measurement error 专家在 panel 上时， Theorem 1\n    的 novelty claim 被直接否定。R² = 0.99 paradoxically 证明了这 IS 一个 known result  （如果是 novel，empirical\n    verification 不该如此 clean）。 Reframe 方向：降级为 \"consistent with classical ME theory,\n    we verify the product-form  identity holds empirically across LLM annotation settings\"，不再\n    claim formal novelty。 关键：reframe 后这个 experiment 仍有价值，因为 \"verifying classical theory\n    holds  in the LLM annotation context\" 是 valid empirical contribution，但需要 proper\n    citation。\n\n    '\n- name: Semi-Synthetic CSS Benchmark\n  plan_id: exp-003\n  description: Semi-synthetic benchmark using TweetEval sentiment with injected CATE\n    structure\n  expected_results:\n    n_subgroups: 4\n    misclass_rates: S0=0.05, S1=0.10, S2=0.15, S3=0.25\n    p_z1_actual: 0.39\n    debiasing_hurts_confirmed: true\n    hb_vs_mle_n100_S3_extreme: +60% RMSE improvement\n    hb_vs_mle_n50_S3_extreme: -57% RMSE (HB worse)\n    boundary_condition: n_expert >= 100\n    reviewer_perceived_validity: low — DGP designed to favor method\n  result_rationale: 'Worst 档下 reviewer 对 exp-003 的攻击角度： (a) \"Semi-synthetic\" DGP 是\n    author-designed：CATE heterogeneity 是 injected 的， misclassification rates 是 hand-picked\n    的，treatment assignment 是 controlled 的 ——  \"the authors designed a DGP where their\n    method works, then showed it works\"； (b) misclass_rates S0=0.05 到 S3=0.25 的 spread（Δπ=0.20）被视为\n    \"optimistic —  real-world Δπ in exp-004 is only 0.117, and in exp-012 pilot is\n    0.098-0.200 depending on grouping\"； (c) P(Z=1)=0.39 被视为 \"unrealistically high\n    — CivilComments P(Z=1)=0.18,  most real datasets have severe class imbalance that\n    exp-003 avoids\"； (d) n=50 boundary condition 被 acknowledged 但 n=100 recommendation\n    被视为  \"will be violated in real per-subgroup settings with K=4+ and small expert\n    budgets\"； (e) 整个 semi-synthetic 在 exp-015/016 negative 面前被 recharacterized 为  \"overfitting\n    to favorable simulation conditions\"。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table 4: Semi-Synthetic Results vs Reviewer Perception'\n    columns:\n    - Config\n    - HB RMSE Δ vs MLE\n    - Actual Validity\n    - Reviewer Perception\n    rows:\n    - - n=50/S3/extreme\n      - -57%\n      - Boundary condition\n      - '\"Method fails at practical budgets\"'\n    - - n=100/S3/extreme\n      - +60%\n      - Strong result\n      - '\"Only works because P(Z=1)=0.39 and symmetric CM\"'\n    - - n=250/S3\n      - +5-17%\n      - Moderate gain\n      - '\"Modest, not worth the complexity\"'\n    - - n=500/all\n      - +0.2-1.6%\n      - Converged\n      - '\"At this budget, any method works\"'\n  figures_description:\n  - RMSE heatmap across n_expert × subgroup — reviewer annotates 'note P(Z=1)=0.39,\n    unrealistic for most applications'\n  analysis: 'exp-003 的 semi-synthetic 结果在 worst 档下被 reframed 为 \"controlled validation  that\n    confirms implementation correctness under favorable conditions\"。 关键问题不是 exp-003\n    结果错误，而是它不能 generalize： 当 P(Z=1) 从 0.39 降到 0.18（real data），per-subgroup expert\n    labels  急剧减少，HB estimation noise 吞没 bias correction gain。 这 exactly 是 exp-015/016\n    观察到的 pattern。Reviewer 将此称为 \"overfitting to simulation\"。\n\n    '\n- name: Real-Data Case Study (Pattern Consistency)\n  plan_id: exp-004\n  description: Real CSS dataset (UC Berkeley Hate Speech) with subgroup-varying LLM\n    misclassification\n  expected_results:\n    dataset: UC Berkeley Measuring Hate Speech\n    n_comments: 2496\n    delta_pi: 0.117\n    global_FNR: 0.533\n    avg_abs_bias_naive: 0.21\n    avg_abs_bias_global: 0.273\n    avg_abs_bias_ec_hte: 0.313\n    ec_hte_worse_than_global: true\n    ec_hte_worse_than_naive: true\n    reviewer_verdict: fatal — method fails on real data\n  result_rationale: '这是 worst 档的 kill shot #2，也是最具破坏力的 evidence。 Reviewer 论证链： (a)\n    EC-HTE avg |bias| = 0.313 > Global 0.273 > Naive 0.21 ——  \"the proposed method\n    is WORST among all options on real data\"； (b) 作者 frame 为 \"inconclusive due to\n    wide bootstrap CIs\"，但 reviewer 反驳： \"wide CIs are themselves evidence of the method''s\n    impracticality —  if you can''t get tight enough CIs to demonstrate improvement\n    on 2496 samples,  the method doesn''t scale to realistic settings\"； (c) global\n    FNR = 53% 被视为 \"typical of real LLM annotation\" 而非 \"edge case\" ——  \"if the method\n    breaks whenever FNR > 0.4, it''s not useful for real NLP tasks  where LLMs systematically\n    under-detect minority categories\"； (d) Δπ = 0.117 is \"moderate, not extreme\" ——\n    \"the method needs extreme heterogeneity  to work, but real heterogeneity is moderate\"；\n    (e) exp-015 (GPT-4.1 CMs) 和 exp-016 (GPT-3.5 CMs) 用 controlled semi-synthetic  确认了\n    same failure pattern —— \"this is not a dataset artifact, it''s a systematic failure\"。\n    Reviewer 会写：\"The real-data evaluation (Section 5.3) is the most informative result  in\n    the paper, and it is negative. EC-HTE produces higher bias than both the naive\n    estimator  and global correction on the UC Berkeley Hate Speech corpus. The authors\n    attribute this  to high FNR, but high FNR is the norm in real LLM annotation tasks,\n    not the exception.  A method that only works when the classifier is already good\n    enough is of limited practical value.\"\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table 5: Real-Data Results — The Fatal Evidence'\n    columns:\n    - Method\n    - Avg |Bias|\n    - Rank\n    - Reviewer Interpretation\n    rows:\n    - - Naive\n      - '0.210'\n      - 1 (best)\n      - '\"Doing nothing is better than the proposed method\"'\n    - - Global Corrected\n      - '0.273'\n      - '2'\n      - '\"Simple baseline outperforms\"'\n    - - EC-HTE (proposed)\n      - '0.313'\n      - 3 (worst)\n      - '\"Method INCREASES bias on real data\"'\n  - name: 'Table 6: Cross-Validation with exp-015/016'\n    columns:\n    - Experiment\n    - Real CMs Source\n    - HB vs Global RMSE\n    - Verdict\n    rows:\n    - - exp-004\n      - UC Berkeley direct\n      - HB worse\n      - '\"Fatal\"'\n    - - exp-015\n      - GPT-4.1 pilot CMs\n      - HB 3-4x worse\n      - '\"Confirmed fatal\"'\n    - - exp-016\n      - GPT-3.5 CMs\n      - HB 3.5-5x worse\n      - '\"Triply confirmed\"'\n  figures_description:\n  - Per-subgroup bias comparison bar chart — EC-HTE bars consistently tallest, devastating\n    visual\n  analysis: 'exp-004 的 negative result 在 worst 档下无法 mitigate，只能 reframe。 Reframe 策略：这个\n    negative result BECOMES the core contribution ——  \"we show that standard corrections\n    fail on real data, and we characterize exactly  why (FNR > 0.4 + P(Z=1) < 0.2\n    → insufficient per-subgroup positive-class expert labels)\"。 这是 \"When Debiasing\n    Hurts\" 的 literal embodiment。 但 reviewer 的反驳是：\"problem identification without solution\n    is not sufficient  for EMNLP main — you''ve shown the problem exists, now what?\"\n\n    '\n- name: Diagnostic Criterion Validation\n  plan_id: exp-005\n  description: 'Diagnostic criterion: Δπ × Δτ predicts when global correction fails'\n  expected_results:\n    subgroup_level_auc: 0.833\n    setting_level_auc: 0.49\n    low_pi_hurt_pct: 84.6\n    reviewer_verdict: contribution failure — AUC 0.49 at actionable level\n  result_rationale: 'Worst 档的 kill shot #3。Reviewer 论证： (a) Setting-level AUC = 0.49\n    是 \"literally worse than random\" ——  \"the diagnostic cannot predict at the level\n    where practitioners need to make decisions  (should I use global or stratified\n    correction for THIS dataset?)\"； (b) Subgroup-level AUC = 0.833 被 dismissed： \"subgroup-level\n    prediction is not actionable — a practitioner doesn''t know true subgroup CATEs  at\n    decision time, so they can''t compute the diagnostic at subgroup level\"； (c) \"84.6%\n    of low-Δπ settings hurt\" 是 \"a marginal distribution, not a prediction\" ——  \"knowing\n    that low heterogeneity settings tend to be hurt by correction is trivially obvious  from\n    the bias identity; the diagnostic adds no information beyond the identity itself\"；\n    (d) exp-028 进一步确认 asymmetric diagnostic 也 fails（overall AUC 0.626, K=2 all zero）；\n    (e) reviewer 会将 Claim 3 标记为 \"not supported by the evidence\" 并要求删除或  大幅 downgrade。\n    Reviewer 会写：\"The diagnostic criterion (Claim 3) is presented as a practical tool,  but\n    its setting-level AUC of 0.49 means it cannot distinguish settings where global\n    correction  helps from those where it hurts. The subgroup-level AUC of 0.833 is\n    not actionable because  the required quantities (true subgroup CATEs) are unknown\n    at decision time.  This contribution should be removed or reformulated as a negative\n    result.\"\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table 7: Diagnostic AUC — Claim vs Evidence'\n    columns:\n    - Level\n    - AUC\n    - Actionable?\n    - Reviewer Verdict\n    rows:\n    - - Subgroup\n      - '0.833'\n      - No (requires true CATE)\n      - '\"Circular — needs what you''re trying to estimate\"'\n    - - Setting\n      - '0.490'\n      - Yes (but fails)\n      - '\"Worse than coin flip\"'\n    - - Asymmetric (exp-028)\n      - 0.611-0.626\n      - 'No'\n      - '\"Marginal improvement, still useless\"'\n  figures_description:\n  - ROC curve at setting level — curve hugs diagonal, visually devastating\n  analysis: 'Diagnostic 在 worst 档下被判定为 complete failure。 Reframe 策略：abandon AUC-based\n    prediction entirely，转为  \"empirical rule of thumb: if Δπ > 0.10, check before applying\n    global correction\"。 这不是 formal diagnostic，而是 practitioner guideline ——  类似 \"if\n    VIF > 10, worry about multicollinearity\" 的 heuristic。 但 reviewer 可能仍会质疑：\"this\n    threshold was derived from your own synthetic data,  how do we know it generalizes?\"\n\n    '\n- name: Expert Label Budget Sensitivity\n  plan_id: exp-006\n  description: Systematic sweep of n_expert × K × regime for crossover point\n  expected_results:\n    crossover_K2_extreme: 250\n    crossover_K2_moderate: never\n    crossover_K4_extreme: 1000\n    crossover_K4_moderate: 2000\n    hb_vs_mle_wins: 21/24 (87.5%)\n    reviewer_verdict: impractical budgets in moderate regime\n  result_rationale: 'Worst 档下 reviewer 的解读： (a) K=2/moderate \"never crosses\" = \"in\n    the most common real-world scenario  (moderate heterogeneity, binary subgroups),\n    EC-HTE NEVER outperforms global on RMSE\"； (b) K=4/extreme crossover at n=1000\n    experts = \"who has 1000 expert-labeled samples  for calibration? At that budget,\n    just use expert labels directly for CATE estimation\"； (c) K=4/moderate crossover\n    at n=2000 = \"absurd — 2000 expert labels for 4 subgroups  means 500/subgroup,\n    at which point expert-only estimation is viable\"； (d) K=2/extreme crossover at\n    n=250 是 \"the only practical scenario,  but extreme heterogeneity is rare in real\n    data (exp-004 Δπ=0.117 is moderate)\"； (e) HB vs MLE 21/24 wins 被 dismissed as\n    \"improvement over the wrong baseline —  the question is HB vs Global, not HB vs\n    MLE\"。 总结：reviewer 将 exp-006 解读为 \"the method''s own budget analysis shows  it''s\n    impractical except in rare extreme-heterogeneity scenarios\"。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table 8: Crossover Points — Reviewer Interpretation'\n    columns:\n    - Config\n    - Crossover n_expert\n    - Practical?\n    - Reviewer Comment\n    rows:\n    - - K=2/extreme\n      - '250'\n      - Marginal\n      - '\"Only practical scenario, but extreme regime is rare\"'\n    - - K=2/moderate\n      - Never\n      - 'No'\n      - '\"Method never helps in common scenario\"'\n    - - K=4/extreme\n      - '1000'\n      - 'No'\n      - '\"Budget exceeds most research projects\"'\n    - - K=4/moderate\n      - '2000'\n      - 'No'\n      - '\"At 2000 labels, use experts directly\"'\n  figures_description:\n  - Crossover curve plot — reviewer highlights the 'never' line for K=2/moderate as\n    paper's self-contradiction\n  analysis: 'exp-006 在 worst 档下成为 \"method''s own evidence against itself\"。 核心问题：EC-HTE\n    的 value proposition 是 \"use LLM labels cheaply + few expert labels for calibration\"，\n    但 crossover analysis 显示 calibration 本身需要大量 expert labels， 侵蚀了 cost-effectiveness\n    argument。 Reframe：转为 \"budget guidelines for practitioners\" —— 不是 \"EC-HTE 需要多少\n    labels\"  而是 \"any correction method 在低 budget 时不如 naive\"。\n\n    '\n- name: PPCI + DSL Baseline Comparison\n  plan_id: exp-007\n  description: PPCI/DSL baselines, EC-HTE+PPCI composition for dual-error scenarios\n  expected_results:\n    dgp_c_extreme_n250_k2_ec_hte_ppci_bias: 0.005\n    dgp_c_extreme_n250_k2_ppci_alone_bias: 0.004\n    dgp_c_extreme_n250_k2_ec_hte_alone_bias: 0.178\n    ec_hte_ppci_rmse: 0.225\n    ppci_alone_rmse: 0.261\n    reviewer_verdict: PPCI alone achieves same bias reduction — why add EC-HTE?\n  result_rationale: 'Worst 档下 reviewer 的 devastating observation： (a) DGP C（both errors）:\n    ec_hte_ppci bias = 0.005, BUT ppci_alone bias = 0.004 ——  \"PPCI alone achieves\n    LOWER bias than the proposed composition! EC-HTE adds nothing to bias reduction\"；\n    (b) RMSE: ec_hte_ppci 0.225 vs ppci_alone 0.261 = 14% improvement， 但 reviewer\n    认为 \"this modest RMSE gain doesn''t justify the additional complexity  of implementing\n    EC-HTE on top of PPCI\"； (c) DGP A（covariate only）: ec_hte works well，但 reviewer\n    质疑： \"how often is covariate error the ONLY error source? In real data, outcome\n    error always exists， making DGP C the relevant scenario — where PPCI alone suffices\"；\n    (d) DSL per-subgroup 作为 baseline 未被 properly compared： \"if DSL per-subgroup achieves\n    comparable results without the HB machinery,  what''s the methodological contribution?\"；\n    (e) \"Composition is necessary and sufficient\" claim 被 weakened to  \"PPCI is sufficient;\n    EC-HTE is optional for modest RMSE gains\"。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table 9: DGP C (Both Errors) — PPCI vs EC-HTE+PPCI'\n    columns:\n    - Method\n    - '|Bias|'\n    - RMSE\n    - Reviewer Verdict\n    rows:\n    - - PPCI alone\n      - '0.004'\n      - '0.261'\n      - '\"Sufficient — simpler, nearly same bias\"'\n    - - EC-HTE+PPCI\n      - '0.005'\n      - '0.225'\n      - '\"Marginal RMSE gain, not worth complexity\"'\n    - - EC-HTE alone\n      - '0.178'\n      - '0.226'\n      - '\"Cannot handle outcome error\"'\n    - - Naive\n      - '0.251'\n      - '0.269'\n      - '\"EC-HTE alone barely beats naive\"'\n  figures_description:\n  - DGP A/B/C comparison panel — reviewer circles DGP C where PPCI alone ≈ EC-HTE+PPCI\n  analysis: 'exp-007 在 worst 档下暴露了 EC-HTE 的 marginal value： 当 PPCI 已经 available 时，EC-HTE\n    的 additional contribution 仅是 14% RMSE reduction。 Reviewer 将此定性为 \"incremental improvement\n    over existing method,  not a new paradigm\"。 Reframe：在 \"When Debiasing Hurts\" 版本中，PPCI\n    comparison  成为 \"what practitioners should use instead\" 的 recommendation。\n\n    '\n- name: Multiple LLM Annotator Comparison\n  plan_id: exp-008\n  description: 6 LLM models (GPT-3.5 through GPT-5.4) measuring misclassification\n    heterogeneity patterns\n  expected_results:\n    models_completed: 6\n    all_delta_pi_above_005: true\n    effective_delta_pi_range: 0.080 - 0.198\n    worst_subgroup_consensus: True_medium (5/6 models)\n    spearman_significant_pairs: 4\n    reviewer_verdict: unsurprising — well-known that different models have different\n      error patterns\n  result_rationale: 'Worst 档下 reviewer 承认 empirical finding 但否定其 significance： (a)\n    \"All 6 models show Δπ > 0.05\" 被视为 \"we already know LLMs have non-uniform error\n    patterns —  Ashwin et al. (2025) documented this, Tornberg (2024) documented this,  the\n    entire LLM-as-annotator literature is built on this observation\"； (b) Δπ range\n    0.080-0.198 被视为 \"moderate, not extreme — confirming that  real-world heterogeneity\n    falls in the regime where EC-HTE doesn''t help (exp-006: K=2/moderate never crosses)\"；\n    (c) \"Structural, not model-specific\" finding 被 reviewer 重新 frame： \"yes, heterogeneity\n    is structural — and it''s structurally MODERATE,  which is exactly the regime\n    where global correction is sufficient\"； (d) 只有 4 subgroups after filtering（excluding\n    n<10），statistical power 有限， Spearman correlations 多数 p>0.20； (e) GPT-5.4 Δπ=0.114\n    被 reviewer 引用为 \"even the best available model  has moderate heterogeneity — confirming\n    that the MODERATE regime is the relevant one\"。 然而在 reframed \"When Debiasing Hurts\"\n    版本中，exp-008 成为 core contribution： 6 models × 3 generations 的 systematic evidence\n    证明 heterogeneity 是 structural phenomenon。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table 10: Cross-Model Δπ — Reviewer Interpretation'\n    columns:\n    - Model\n    - Generation\n    - Effective Δπ\n    - Reviewer Comment\n    rows:\n    - - GPT-3.5-turbo\n      - Gen 1\n      - '0.198'\n      - '\"Oldest model, most error — unsurprising\"'\n    - - GPT-4-turbo\n      - Gen 2\n      - '0.149'\n      - '\"Better model, less error — unsurprising\"'\n    - - GPT-4.1\n      - Gen 2\n      - '0.098'\n      - '\"Moderate — in the regime where EC-HTE doesn''t help\"'\n    - - GPT-4o\n      - Gen 2\n      - '0.080'\n      - '\"Low — global correction sufficient\"'\n    - - GPT-4o-mini\n      - Gen 2\n      - '0.136'\n      - '\"Small model, more error — expected\"'\n    - - GPT-5.4\n      - Gen 3\n      - '0.114'\n      - '\"Latest model still has moderate heterogeneity\"'\n  figures_description:\n  - Bar chart of Δπ across 6 models, ordered by generation — reviewer notes downward\n    trend as evidence 'problem is diminishing with model improvement'\n  analysis: 'exp-008 在 worst 档下有双重解读： (1) Reviewer 可以 argue \"heterogeneity is diminishing\n    with model generations  (GPT-3.5: 0.198 → GPT-5.4: 0.114), so the problem is self-solving\"；\n    (2) 但在 reframed paper 中，这 IS the contribution：systematic evidence  across 6 models\n    showing heterogeneity persists even in latest generation。 关键防御：Δπ=0.114 for GPT-5.4\n    仍然 above the threshold（0.10） where bias amplification is non-trivial。\n\n    '\n- name: Adaptive Expert Annotation Allocation\n  plan_id: exp-009\n  description: CATE-weighted allocation targeting high-CATE × high-error subgroups\n  expected_results:\n    status: not completed (P2 priority, cut from submission)\n    reviewer_reaction: missing experiment noted but not fatal\n    hypothetical_if_run:\n      improvement_over_uniform: 10-15% RMSE reduction in high-error subgroups\n      aggregate_improvement: 5-8% overall\n      still_worse_than_global_in_moderate: true\n  result_rationale: 'Worst 档下 exp-009 大概率未完成（P2 priority，5-day deadline 内无法实现）。 Reviewer\n    反应分两种： (a) 如果提到但未完成：\"the authors mention adaptive allocation as future work,  but\n    this would be necessary to make the method practical — without it,  the budget\n    requirements (exp-006) are prohibitive\"； (b) 如果完全不提：reviewer 不会注意到缺失，因为 exp-009\n    不是 core claim 的 evidence。 即使 exp-009 完成，worst 档 reviewer 仍会 argue： \"adaptive allocation\n    improves EC-HTE but doesn''t change the fundamental conclusion —  the method requires\n    too many expert labels to be practical\"。 在 reframed paper 中，exp-009 可以作为 appendix-level\n    future direction， 但不影响 core empirical contribution。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table 11: Adaptive Allocation (Hypothetical)'\n    columns:\n    - Allocation\n    - Aggregate RMSE\n    - High-Error Subgroup RMSE\n    - Reviewer Verdict\n    rows:\n    - - Uniform\n      - '0.12'\n      - '0.18'\n      - '\"Baseline\"'\n    - - CATE-weighted\n      - '0.11'\n      - '0.15'\n      - '\"Modest improvement, doesn''t fix fundamental issue\"'\n    - - Uncertainty-only\n      - '0.115'\n      - '0.16'\n      - '\"Similar to CATE-weighted\"'\n  figures_description:\n  - Not generated — experiment cut from submission\n  analysis: 'exp-009 的缺失在 worst 档下不是 major weakness，因为 reviewer 的 attack vector  是\n    \"method doesn''t work on real data\" 而非 \"method could be improved with adaptive\n    allocation\"。 Cutting exp-009 is correct under time constraints。\n\n    '\n- name: Robustness to Misspecified Subgroup Structure\n  plan_id: exp-010\n  description: Test EC-HTE when subgroups are noisy/overlapping\n  expected_results:\n    k2_coverage_hb_noise0: 0.958\n    k2_coverage_hb_noise50: 0.945\n    k4_coverage_hb_noise0: 0.956\n    k4_coverage_hb_noise50: 0.946\n    graceful_convergence: true\n    hb_beats_mle_all_configs: true\n    reviewer_verdict: trivial result — HB shrinkage is known to be robust\n  result_rationale: 'Worst 档下 reviewer 对 exp-010 的评价： (a) \"Coverage maintained at\n    94.5-95.8% across all noise levels\" 被视为  \"this is the well-known property of hierarchical\n    Bayesian shrinkage —  it automatically pools toward the global estimate when subgroup\n    signal is noisy,  providing an automatic safeguard. This is not a finding, it''s\n    a property of the method\"； (b) \"Graceful convergence to global at 50% noise\" 是\n    \"by construction —  when subgroup labels are random, HB posterior concentrates\n    on the global mean.  This is Definition 1 of partial pooling\"； (c) reviewer 不会\n    flag exp-010 as weakness，但 also 不会 credit it as contribution ——  it''s \"expected\n    behavior, properly verified but not interesting\"； (d) 在 worst 档下，exp-010 的 robustness\n    evidence 被 counter-argued by  exp-015/016/030：\"robust to noise is not the same\n    as robust to real-world conditions —  the method gracefully degrades to Global\n    (the thing it was supposed to beat)\"。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table 12: Robustness — Coverage Across Noise Levels'\n    columns:\n    - Noise Level\n    - K=2 HB Coverage\n    - K=4 HB Coverage\n    - Reviewer Comment\n    rows:\n    - - 0%\n      - '0.958'\n      - '0.956'\n      - '\"Nominal — as expected\"'\n    - - 10%\n      - '0.948'\n      - '0.958'\n      - '\"Robust — as expected from HB\"'\n    - - 25%\n      - '0.950'\n      - '0.960'\n      - '\"Still nominal — standard shrinkage property\"'\n    - - 50%\n      - '0.945'\n      - '0.946'\n      - '\"Converges to global — by construction\"'\n  figures_description:\n  - Coverage vs noise level — flat line, 'reassuring but uninformative' per reviewer\n  analysis: 'exp-010 在 worst 档下是 neutral evidence：不帮助也不伤害。 Reviewer 认为 robustness\n    to subgroup noise 是 \"expected baseline behavior,  not a contribution\"。在 reframed\n    paper 中可以保留在 appendix  作为 \"implementation validation\" 但不宜放在 main text。\n\n    '\n- name: Causal Forest Integration\n  plan_id: exp-011\n  description: 'EC-HTE with CausalForestDML: bias reduction + debiasing-hurts amplification'\n  expected_results:\n    mean_abs_bias_naive: 0.1558\n    mean_abs_bias_global: 0.1073\n    mean_abs_bias_ec_hte: 0.0608\n    mean_rmse_naive: 0.1782\n    mean_rmse_global: 0.1659\n    mean_rmse_ec_hte: 0.2289\n    debiasing_hurts_max_ratio: 5.9\n    debiasing_hurts_cases: 9\n    reviewer_verdict: bias-variance tradeoff unfavorable — RMSE 38% worse than global\n  result_rationale: 'Worst 档下 reviewer 对 exp-011 的解读高度 adversarial： (a) EC-HTE RMSE\n    = 0.2289 vs Global RMSE = 0.1659 —— \"EC-HTE has 38% HIGHER RMSE  than global correction\n    when combined with CausalForest. Lower bias comes at  unacceptable variance cost\"；\n    (b) \"A practitioner cares about RMSE (combined bias + variance), not bias alone.  EC-HTE\n    trades manageable bias for enormous variance, making estimates LESS useful\"； (c)\n    5.9x debiasing-hurts ratio 被 dual-interpreted： reviewer 承认 \"global correction\n    can dramatically amplify bias with CausalForest\"  但 adds \"EC-HTE doesn''t fix\n    this — it has even worse RMSE, just distributed differently  (lower bias, higher\n    variance)\"； (d) 9 cases of debiasing-hurts 在 144 total rows = 6.25%，被视为  \"rare\n    enough that practitioners can detect and handle manually\"； (e) K=2/n=500 near-zero\n    bias（0.004-0.013）被 acknowledged 但  \"at n=500 per subgroup, the expert budget is\n    no longer small —  1000+ experts for 2 subgroups exceeds most research budgets\"。\n    Reviewer 会写：\"Table 4 reveals that EC-HTE''s bias reduction comes at a steep  variance\n    cost: mean RMSE increases 38% compared to global correction (0.229 vs 0.166).  For\n    practitioners who care about prediction accuracy (not just unbiasedness),  this\n    tradeoff is unfavorable. The 5.9x debiasing-hurts ratio for K=4/extreme  is concerning\n    but occurs in only 6% of configurations.\"\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table 13: CausalForest — Bias vs RMSE Tradeoff'\n    columns:\n    - Method\n    - Mean |Bias|\n    - Mean RMSE\n    - RMSE Rank\n    - Reviewer Verdict\n    rows:\n    - - Naive\n      - '0.156'\n      - '0.178'\n      - '2'\n      - '\"Higher bias but lower RMSE than EC-HTE\"'\n    - - Global\n      - '0.107'\n      - '0.166'\n      - 1 (best)\n      - '\"Best RMSE, acceptable bias\"'\n    - - EC-HTE\n      - '0.061'\n      - '0.229'\n      - 3 (worst)\n      - '\"Lowest bias but worst RMSE — unfavorable tradeoff\"'\n  - name: 'Table 14: Debiasing-Hurts Cases with CausalForest'\n    columns:\n    - Config\n    - Global/Naive Bias Ratio\n    - Frequency\n    - Reviewer Comment\n    rows:\n    - - K=4/extreme/sg0\n      - 5.9x\n      - 1/144\n      - '\"Rare extreme case\"'\n    - - K=4/extreme/sg1-3\n      - 1.2-2.1x\n      - 8/144\n      - '\"Moderate, manageable\"'\n    - - All other configs\n      - <1.0x\n      - 135/144\n      - '\"Global correction works fine 94% of the time\"'\n  figures_description:\n  - Bias-RMSE scatterplot with method colors — EC-HTE in Pareto-dominated region (low\n    bias, high RMSE)\n  analysis: exp-011 在 worst 档下强化了 \"method works in theory, fails in practice\" narrative：\n    即使在 synthetic DGP 上，EC-HTE 的 RMSE 比 global 差 38%。 Reviewer 将此解读为 \"the fundamental\n    tradeoff is unfavorable —  per-subgroup CM estimation noise exceeds the bias correction\n    benefit\"。 在 reframed paper 中，5.9x debiasing-hurts 成为 core empirical finding： \"CausalForest\n    amplifies the debiasing-hurts effect\" 是 novel observation， 但需要 frame 为 \"warning\n    to practitioners\" 而非 \"EC-HTE solves this\"。\n","numLines":724,"startLine":1,"totalLines":724}}}
